151	 * marks, 2026-08-11) may take before it reaches public HTML inside a `style=""` attribute — the
152	 * same "collapse anything unrecognized rather than splice an arbitrary string into markup"
153	 * discipline {@link safeHref} applies to link hrefs (C7), adapted for CSS instead of a URL scheme.
154	 *
155	 * Accepts: 3/4/6/8-digit hex (`#abc`, `#aabbcc`, `#aabbccdd`); a bare alphabetic keyword up to 20
156	 * chars (`red`, `transparent`, `currentcolor` — an unrecognized keyword is simply invalid CSS the
157	 * browser ignores, not an injection vector, so this doesn't need a fixed keyword allowlist); or one
158	 * of the five functional notations Tiptap's own Color/Highlight pickers can produce (`rgb`/`rgba`/
159	 * `hsl`/`hsla`/`oklch`), with the characters INSIDE the parens restricted to digits/`%`/`.`/`,`/
160	 * whitespace/`/` (the last for `oklch(l c h / a)`'s alpha slot) — no nested `(`, no `url(`, no `;`,
161	 * no backslash, so nothing here can break out of the `style` attribute's value or smuggle a second
162	 * CSS declaration. Returns `null` (not `"#"` — there is no safe placeholder color to fall back to)
163	 * so every caller omits the attribute entirely on a rejected value, same as {@link renderImageTag}'s
164	 * own "omit rather than emit a malformed/placeholder attribute" rule.
