 11	 * is the direct counterpart of `liquid-allowlist.ts` and keeps the surface to
 12	 * pure, non-I/O, non-dynamic logic. Enforcement walks the *parsed AST*
 13	 * (`Handlebars.parse()`), not the raw source text, so a helper name appearing
 14	 * inside a string literal or an HTML comment can neither trigger a false
 15	 * positive nor slip past as a false negative.
 16	 *
 17	 * Why an allowlist is load-bearing HERE specifically. Handlebars' historical
 18	 * CVE record (CVE-2019-19919, CVE-2021-23369, CVE-2021-23383 and relatives) is
 19	 * a record of *compiling attacker-controlled template strings* — the exact
 20	 * thing this tier does by design — escaping into prototype pollution and then
 21	 * remote code execution. Those specific bugs are fixed in the pinned 4.7.x
 22	 * line, but the shape of the risk is structural, not incidental: a template
 23	 * language whose compiler emits JavaScript will keep finding new ways for
 24	 * template text to reach the compiler's own object graph. Three constructs
 25	 * carry essentially all of that risk and all three are refused outright below
 26	 * rather than filtered:
 27	 *   - `{{{triple-stash}}}` / `{{&amp;stash}}` raw output (the XSS seam),
 28	 *   - `{{> partial}}` / `{{#> partial-block}}` (the partial-registry read,
 29	 *     Handlebars' analogue of Liquid's `include`/`render` filesystem tags),
 30	 *   - `{{#*inline}}` / `{{*decorator}}` (decorators, which mutate the
 31	 *     runtime's own program/partial resolution from inside a template).
 32	 *
 33	 * How it relates to the project:
 34	 * Called from the same two sites the Liquid allowlist is, matching ADR-020
 35	 * §3's "lint before publish" + "defensive at render time" pair:
 36	 *   - `features/theme/theme.ts`'s `loadTheme()` — lint every `.hbs`/
 37	 *     `.handlebars` file at discovery time, folding violations into the
 38	 *     existing `errors`/`status: "invalid"` mechanism.
 39	 *   - `server/http/site/handlebars-worker.ts` — a second, redundant check
 40	 *     immediately before render, in case a template was hot-edited on disk
 41	 *     after a theme was validated (`loadTheme`'s result is not re-verified
