511	 * Deliberately does NOT scan `post.bodyJson` for every distinct `transformName` an author's doc
512	 * might reference (the way `resolveHtmlPageEmbeds` scans a Page's `body_html` for embed ids):
513	 * `registerTransform` has exactly one caller anywhere in this codebase
514	 * (`ensureCoreMediaTransform`, `server/deps.ts`'s boot chain), which only ever registers
515	 * `CORE_PUBLIC_TRANSFORM_NAME` — there is no OTHER registered name a real ref could resolve
516	 * against yet, so a single-name lookup is behavior-identical to a full scan at today's real
517	 * scale. A second core-declared transform (`thumb`, `hero`, ...) would need this widened to a
518	 * real scan, same as the widget/html-embed resolvers already do for their own multi-id case —
519	 * disclosed here rather than silently assumed permanent.
520	 *
521	 * Returns an empty map (not a thrown error) when the transform is not yet registered (a
522	 * mid-boot race, or a workspace this hasn't run for) — `renderDocNode`'s `image` case already
