 17	/**
 18	 * @file Path containment and file I/O for the `themes` agent-tool domain
 19	 * (`agent-tools.ts`).
 20	 *
 21	 * Purpose:
 22	 * The `themes` domain exposes a deliberately broad capability — read and write
 23	 * ANY file inside ONE theme's own folder — on the argument that theme content's
 24	 * real safety boundary is the runtime validation every theme goes through
 25	 * regardless of authorship (the Liquid/Handlebars allowlists, worker isolation,
 26	 * the declarative tier's closed JSON vocabulary). That argument holds only for
 27	 * as long as "inside one theme's own folder" is actually true. This module is
 28	 * where that is made true, and it is the only place in the domain that resolves
 29	 * a caller-supplied string into a filesystem path.
 30	 *
 31	 * Why containment is not a string prefix check. The obvious implementation —
 32	 * `resolved.startsWith(themeDir)` — is wrong in three separate ways, each
 33	 * independently exploitable:
 34	 *   1. It admits a SIBLING directory whose name extends the base's:
 35	 *      `themes/handlebars/ledger-evil/x` starts with `themes/handlebars/ledger`.
 36	 *      Comparing against `themeDir + sep` fixes only this one.
 37	 *   2. It compares the wrong string when the input has not been normalized.
 38	 *      `themes/ledger/../../../etc/passwd` must be resolved BEFORE any
 39	 *      comparison, not after.
 40	 *   3. It is blind to symlinks. A `.hbs` file (or a directory) inside the theme
 41	 *      folder that links to `/etc` passes every lexical check ever written,
 42	 *      because lexically it really is inside the folder.
 43	 * {@link resolveThemeFilePath} handles all three: it resolves first, compares
 44	 * with `path.relative` (which cannot be fooled by a name-prefix sibling), and
 45	 * then re-checks against the `realpath` of the deepest ancestor that actually
 46	 * exists on disk — which is what catches a symlink escape for a file that does
 47	 * not exist yet, the case a write must handle.
 48	 *
 49	 * How it relates to the project:
 50	 * Used only by `tool-registrations.ts`'s handlers. Nothing else in the codebase
 51	 * writes theme files at runtime.
 52	 */
